webrick-crlf-2017-17742-2019-16254 — reproduction log
=====================================================
Class: CRLF / HTTP response-header injection / response splitting (CWE-113)
Product: Ruby WEBrick (github.com/ruby/webrick, bundled in Ruby MRI 2.5.x stdlib)
Pair: CVE-2017-17742 (V1 incomplete fix = TARGET) -> CVE-2019-16254 (V2 complete)
Oracle: Variant A (same regular-header sink; original = CRLF pair, residual = isolated LF)

VERSION PINS (verified by grepping the BUNDLED webrick httpresponse.rb inside each image)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why ruby:2.5.x base images, not the webrick gem: the standalone webrick gem tags jump
straight from v1.4.2 (NO check_header) to v1.4.4 (the COMPLETE /[\r\n]/ check) — there is
NO gem tag carrying the incomplete /\r\n/-only state. That state existed ONLY in Ruby MRI's
in-tree bundled webrick (still versioned 1.4.2) shipped in ruby 2.5.1 .. 2.5.6.

  V0 = ruby:2.5.0-slim  webrick 1.4.2  -> send_header has NO check_header  (pre CVE-2017-17742)
       (grep: "NO check_header")
  V1 = ruby:2.5.1-slim  webrick 1.4.2  -> def check_header(v); if v =~ /\r\n/ then raise; ...   [TARGET]
  V2 = ruby:2.5.8-slim  webrick 1.4.2  -> def check_header(v); v=v.to_s; if /[\r\n]/ =~ v then raise; ...

check_header CR/LF-check EVOLUTION (verbatim from bundled httpresponse.rb):
  V0: (method absent)
  V1: if header_value =~ /\r\n/        # rejects the CR-LF PAIR only; lone \r or \n slips through
  V2: if /[\r\n]/ =~ header_value      # rejects ANY isolated CR or LF (char class)
On InvalidHeader, send_header rescues -> @header.clear; @cookies.clear; set_error; retry
=> a blocked payload yields a 500 error page WITHOUT the injected flag line.

PAYLOADS (query ?x=<value>, WEBrick %XX-decodes it into the X-Reflected header value)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  original (CVE-2017-17742):  "pcbseed\r\nX-Pcb-Injected: <FLAG>"   (full CR-LF pair, %0d%0a)
  residual (CVE-2019-16254):  "pcbseed\nX-Pcb-Injected: <FLAG>"     (isolated LF, %0a)
Same sink (regular response header X-Reflected), same CR/LF char class; the incompleteness is
the missed CHARACTER FORM (isolated CR/LF vs the CRLF pair) — matches the ruby-lang advisory:
"The previous fix was incomplete, which addressed the CRLF vector, but did not address an
 isolated CR or an isolated LF."

GATE (flag_oracle.validate_case, Variant A) — real Docker, PCBFLAG_ef5de24291088a42735fdc1596b24711
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 : true    (V0 no guard -> CRLF split lands, flag in raw bytes)
  original_poc_blocked_on_v1      : true    (V1 /\r\n/ matches the pair -> 500, flag absent)
  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1   : true    (V1 /\r\n/ MISSES lone \n -> split lands, flag in raw bytes)  <-- RESIDUAL
  passed                          : true
  data-quality extras:
  original_blocked_on_v2          : true    (V2 /[\r\n]/ rejects the pair)
  bypass_blocked_on_v2            : true    (V2 /[\r\n]/ rejects the isolated LF -> residual closed)
  residual_reaches_flag_on_v0     : true    (isolated LF also splits on the unguarded V0)
  _env_ready: {v0: true, v1: true, v2: true}

VERDICT: GATE PASSED. Genuine incomplete-fix pair (not a reject):
  distinct base images/versions (2.5.0 / 2.5.1 / 2.5.8), distinct fix commits
  (7018305 vs 8658b1b), V1 != V0 (V1 adds check_header), original (\r\n pair) differs from
  residual (isolated \n), V1 blocks original but NOT residual, V2 blocks BOTH.

